  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This baby ear-flap hat is worked with the ear flaps knitted first then joined into the cast-on round, sized for Baby (38 cm head), Toddler (46 cm), and Child (50 cm)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The ear flaps are worked flat first then folded into the cast-on round, so their size is locked in before the body begins. This method produces a seamless join at the flap base. A "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "m1"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "M1"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " increase (lift the bar between stitches and knit through the back loop) shapes each flap from a narrow cast-on to a wider working edge. The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-loop"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic loop"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " method handles the small circumference once the flaps are joined. About 80 g (Baby) to 120 g (Child) of superwash aran yarn."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "heading": "Materials",
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "Superwash aran-weight wool yarn",
              "qty": "80 g (Baby) / 100 g (Toddler) / 120 g (Child)",
              "substitutions": "Superwash required for machine washing"
            },
            {
              "name": "5 mm circular needle, 80 cm (UK 6 / US 8)",
              "qty": "1",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "4.5 mm circular needle, 80 cm (UK 7 / US 7) -- for brim",
              "qty": "1",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "Stitch markers",
              "qty": "9 (1 BOR + 8 crown)",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "Tapestry needle and scissors",
              "qty": "1 each",
              "substitutions": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "18 sts x 24 rounds = 10 x 10 cm in stocking stitch on 5 mm needles, blocked. For the Baby size, at 19 sts per 10 cm the hat is 36 cm -- slightly small. Adjust needle if knitting for a newborn."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pattern"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Before you cast on, circle your size -- every count reads Baby (Toddler, Child)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ear flaps (make 2)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "On the 5 mm needle, cast on 4 sts using long-tail cast-on. Tail formula: tail_cm = (needle mm x stitch count) / 10 + 15. For 4 sts on 5 mm: (5 x 4) / 10 + 15 = 17 cm. Row 1 (RS): k1, "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "m1"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "M1"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", k to last st, M1, k1. Row 2 (WS): k1, p to last st, k1. Repeat rows 1 and 2 until 14 (16, 18) sts. Work 2 rows straight. Leave on needle or holder."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Join and cast on"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "On the 4.5 mm needle, using long-tail cast-on, cast on 20 (26, 28) sts for the back of the hat. Knit across the 14 (16, 18) sts of the first ear flap. Cast on 6 (10, 12) sts for the front. Knit across the 14 (16, 18) sts of the second ear flap. Cast on 14 (16, 16) sts to complete the back. Join into the round without twisting, place BOR marker. Total sts: 68 (84, 92). After joining, you should have 68 (84, 92) stitches on the needle."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Brim"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work 8 rounds of 2 x 2 rib: *k2, p2; repeat. Switch to 5 mm needle."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Body"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work in stocking stitch until hat measures 12 (16, 18) cm from cast-on edge."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Crown shaping"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Place 8 markers dividing sts into 8 equal sections."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Decrease round 1: *k to 2 sts before marker, k2tog; repeat from * 8 times. 60 (76, 84) sts."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Round 2: knit all."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Continue alternating until 24 sts, then every round until 8 sts remain."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "After the final decrease round, you should have 8 stitches on the needle, ready to gather."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Top finish"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cut yarn with 20 cm tail. Draw through all 8 sts, pull firmly, fasten on inside."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Common faults"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ear flaps unequal: both flaps must be worked to the same row count before joining. Count rows on each before proceeding to the join round."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gap at flap join: the transition from flap stitches to cast-on stitches can gap. Pick up and knit 1 stitch in the join gap on the brim round and k2tog with the adjacent stitch to close it."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Flaps too wide: the Baby ear flaps are 14 sts and are proportioned for a 38 cm head. If the baby has a smaller head, reduce the number of M1 increase rows by one pair."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Weave in all ends. Block over a small bowl, pinning the ear flaps flat and downward while damp."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Machine wash cool gentle cycle. Reshape and dry flat with ear flaps spread."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The warm ear-flap hat uses the same construction in adult sizes for a matching family set."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}